WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
It's not written in the Talmud, this ceremony is not written in the Talmud, no claim.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.400
It's a part of the ceremony of the custom of the Jewish people, specifically the Sephardic people have the custom,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:15.200
which is a very beautiful custom, in which we declare that we believe that this Sefer Torah is the Sefer Torah of the Al-Qaeda.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.200
And why do we have to, and why the Sephardic people they do this more than other people? I'll tell you why.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:27.200
The Muslims, they say that we forged the Torah. Do you know this? Why?

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.920
Because in the Torah, as it is written,

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:31.700
Ishaq is the son of Sarah,

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.480
and Ishmael is the son of the concubine.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.640
So they say, this is a forgery.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.320
You Jews, you forged the Torah.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:40.580
So therefore we say,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:46.620
I don't know whether it's clear what I'm trying to...

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:53.080
Yes, we assert that we believe that this is...

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.380
But that's the point, you know.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.700
Moshi Rabbeinu got it from Mubarak when he went up to Al-Tinai, right?

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:01.200
No!

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:01.700
What's that?

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:05.200
Oh, that's important. How did he get it and what did he get?

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.700
Now, and this is already more than one opinion.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.700
The opinion that I accept, this is my man's opinion, that of Rabbeinu Sa'adiya,

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.700
the opinion is the following.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.200
He got messages of the Torah,

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.700
Baidya Beda Hashem, Moshe de Mor, you know, go and tell them to succeed.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.700
Go and tell them to do this, go and tell them to do this.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:30.700
And Moshe Rabbeinu at that time would write or would teach the people orally what the Torah is.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:40.700
No, but at that time during the 40 years, the 40 years of the desert when there were, you know, there was no Sefer Torah yet.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:50.700
The Sefer Torah was write before it's dead. Before it's dead, G-d told him, now from Bereshit to Rehenei Korosh Hashanah I'm going to return to you the whole Torah.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:56.200
and right before his death he gave him the Sefer Torah, Moshe Rabbeinu.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:02.700
In other words, the 40 years of the desert there was no Sefer Torah, there was only...

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.700
Laws.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:07.700
That's not true, that's a tradition.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:13.700
That's why I said, and this is more than, I mentioned, I said this, I said there's more than one opinion on this.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:21.700
My opinion of Rambam is that this was the Torah, the Sefer Torah was given only before the Torah.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.700
You know, it was the Sefer Torah.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.700
It was given by God to him and he wrote it.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:26.700
Yes.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.700
And this was...

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:28.700
And the same person.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.700
Yes. And God, because Moshe is not the author.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:32.700
No.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:33.700
Because God is the author.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:34.700
What happened before he made the Torah?

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.700
Oh, so that is the point of the deal.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.700
During the 40 years, there was no Torah that was written.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.320
with only Torah shebe'afet, oral tradition.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.420
And from here the rabbis,

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:46.560
like Haram Bam,

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.340
he says, from here we learn

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:51.500
that oral tradition,

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:52.920
according to Jewish law,

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.660
has precedence over

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:56.440
written law.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.500
Because the Torah was known

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:02.580
before orally,

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.160
and after it was put into writing.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:06.740
And this is, again,

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.880
because the Christians say,

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.620
and the Karahites and other people

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.940
We say, well, yes, we accept the Pentateuch, yes, or the Torah, but we interpret it our own way.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.680
So we say, no, you can't interpret the Torah your own way.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.860
You have to interpret the Torah according to the tradition.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.340
They say, well, what do we mean tradition?

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.040
We don't want to accept tradition.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:30.480
So we say, no, well, tradition has precedence over the Torah.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:35.640
The Torah first was known as Torah Sheveh Al-Beh, was known orally.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:43.640
For instance, like Sa'ad Ya Gaon, he has a book that he wrote in Arabic, you know what it translated?

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:48.640
It's Kitab al-Anwar wal-Maraqi. And it's a very interesting book.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:52.640
And then, in this book, he says, and he says like this, he says,

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:58.640
it's obviously that what is binding according to Jewish religion, the most binding is the Oral Law.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.640
God spoke the Ten Commandments.

