By Chal Elohim, By Yom HaShem Ye'im Melech Tor HaSheh HaTzach.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:36.320
By the fact that God, by creating the Yom HaShavei, God finished all His work.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:37.680
Yes, sir?

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:40.280
Vaykar refers to Vayom HaShavei.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.540
Vaykar Elohim Vayom HaShavei.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:42.640
Yes?

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:46.980
By making the Yom HaShavei, God finished all His work.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:48.120
Do you understand?

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:48.600
Do you understand?

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:52.300
That the Yom Shabbat is part of the original creation,

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:58.480
and that Yom Shabbat is the crowning completion of the whole creation.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:12:59.220
Alright?

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:02.140
So there are two explanations. The first explanation is Peshat.

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:05.740
And the second is a little bit more deeper.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:09.800
You could extract either or both, or perhaps none.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.620
It can't be neither. The seventh day itself is a creation.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:15.380
That's why.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.820
Therefore, there has to have been a man, even though...

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:20.700
Yes, he created the Yom HaShem Him.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:24.980
That's right. This is one explanation which is according to Kabbalah.

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:28.080
And I think it makes a little bit of sense.

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:31.460
But this happened to be written by the Hashem.

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:32.900
Okay, but doesn't it have to be?

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:35.460
Because you can't take away that the seventh day was forbidden.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:36.980
Yes, but...

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:37.780
Yes, go on.

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:38.900
Yes, sir.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:42.500
Did Yom HaShavu'i stop for Friday night sound down?

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:43.860
Friday night sound down, yes.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:45.780
Now,

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:50.980
V'yish'vod v'yom haShavu'i mikol me'ach tov ha'sha.

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:53.940
And thus, in the seventh day, God rested.

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:55.780
What does it mean rested in Hebrew?

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:58.580
Dishvot in Hebrew doesn't mean rested like in English.

00:13:58.680 --> 00:13:59.940
And that's important to understand.

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:04.120
Dishvot in English to rest means that you're tired.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:06.680
And rest is a positive verb.

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:08.100
In other words, and you rest.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.320
In Hebrew, by ishvot, it's a negative word.

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.220
It means to abstain of doing something.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:16.480
So by ishvot, by Yom HaKevi'i, means that.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.960
It means God abstained in the seven days,

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:22.980
of doing any other work.

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:33.300
You know, it doesn't mean that God rested on the seventh day, but rather that God abstained from doing any particular action or creation.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.920
Oh, the difference is enormous.

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:47.240
Rested supposes that somebody is tired, and therefore physical exhaustion, and then you rest.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:50.680
But in Vayishvot doesn't mean to rest in that tent.

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:54.960
Nivu Vayishvot means to abstain from doing something.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:58.940
Shabbat means to abstain from doing things.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:01.200
Now comes the next word.

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:07.460
So now, Vayishvot Vayom HaShiv'i Mikul Merach Tov HaSheh HaTzah.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.640
God abstained from doing things.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.680
Vayimot Ech Elohim Mitum HaShem Echim.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.620
And God made a special blessing for the Yom HaShiv'i.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:21.940
by katechotoh and God declared us to be kadosh what does it mean in Hebrew kadosh?

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:30.620
separate different we say to God atakadosh what do we mean by saying atakadosh?

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:38.420
we say that God you are different because we cannot describe that with positive terms how

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:43.940
could you describe that could you say to God you are good the word good for you means something

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:44.880
that is basically human.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:47.800
Something when you say somebody

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.900
is a good man means that he behaves

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.580
because he has an interest or he has this

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.860
but God is, you know, transcends goodness.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:55.280
How could you describe God?

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:57.840
The best description of God is

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.880
Kadosh. Kadosh means

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:01.540
you are different than anything we know.

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:04.160
That's why we say Kadosh, Kadosh,

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:05.860
Kadosh. You know why we say

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:06.780
three times Kadosh?

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.300
So this, you see,

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:13.440
God is different

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:23.120
you know there are three types of creation. There is the earth which is material and it has a

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:36.160
beginning and also could be destroyed by God. It has an end. Then we have human beings who are

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:42.460
partially are spiritual, partially spiritual but we have a beginning and we

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:49.460
an end. Then there is the Malachim who are spiritual, they have no end, they will never be destroyed, but they have a beginning.

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:54.460
So therefore we say, Kadosh, first be Kadosh, you are different in this material world.

00:16:54.460 --> 00:17:01.460
Why? Because God is neither material, nor has a beginning, nor has an end.

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:10.460
Then Kadosh, you are also different than the intermediate world, the human world, in the sense that, because, alright, you are not material,

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:14.680
And also, we have an end. God, for Abraham, has an end.

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:21.840
Also, Kadosh, Kadosh, Kadosh, also the Malachim, the highest Malachim, also they say to God, Kadosh. Why?

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:29.460
Because although they are immortal, they will never perish, and they are spiritual, still they are created, and God is not created.

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:33.880
So each one, so that's why the Gemara says in one place that there are three worlds.

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:36.080
the lower world

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:37.500
says kadosh, kadosh, kadosh

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:39.180
there is another world that says kadosh, kadosh

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.660
and the highest malachim who say only once kadosh

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.980
because the difference between them and Borei Olam

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:45.480
is basically one

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:47.340
in the sense that Borei Olam

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:49.740
is a creator

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:50.880
and they are creators

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:53.360
we say it like

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:55.740
the three different

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:57.520
I tell you why

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:58.240
because we have

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:00.200
it's a good question

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.700
because we have the three worlds together

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:13.700
Part of us is like the Malachim, part of us is like the material, and part of us is like the secondary world.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:17.700
That's true. We have the three worlds, we have it in us. Maybe that's the reason, I don't know.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:19.700
So now,

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:24.700
And why

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:30.800
He stopped from doing any kind of work

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:35.380
Two explanations

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:38.200
One which I consider Peshat and the other I consider Adelah

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:41.940
God created this world

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:43.560
But this world

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:47.160
Will always continue to reproduce

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:48.280
Whatever God did

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:50.100
Now it's

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:50.960
bara Elohim,

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:53.680
en bara otoh la'asot,

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:56.140
that this world always will continue repeating

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:58.320
the same thing that God made to it.

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:02.620
Now, if the laws that God made into the universe,

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:04.040
that will be la'asot,

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:05.160
always will be continued,

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:05.700
perpetual,

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:08.140
to go over and over and over.

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:10.500
That is the simple expression I said,

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:11.700
bara Elohim,

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:12.860
la'asot,

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:15.560
to make itself over and over to repeat itself.

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.140
That's one expression which I consider to be good.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:18.760
Another expression which is nice is,

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:35.760
I said, but I know him. But now it's up to men, the soul. Now God created the universe, but we have to act in this universe. I don't know whether it's clear that explanation or not. Now, before we have to do something also.

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:57.920
Since Shabbat is such an important Mishva, and since the explanation of Shabbat is written

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:05.380
in this Yoke Sukkim, and since we read this every time, at least once a week, I think

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:09.140
that it is proper for us to try to understand what it says here.

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:11.380
It's starting very, very deep.

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:16.380
It says like this.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:24.340
Gentlemen,

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:27.380
I say,

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:30.000
I tell you why.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:30.860
What does it say here?

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:32.300
Here it says,

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:36.500
that God created the world in six days,

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.920
stopped from doing work at the seventh,

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:41.320
and that's why he made the Yom Kippur.

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.040
What does it mean to me like this?

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:44.660
Something very, very important.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:52.760
It means that when we observe the Jabbah, we assert, we declare that we, in point of

00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:57.760
fact, we believe that God created the world and He stopped in the sixth and seventh day.

00:20:57.760 --> 00:21:01.760
It means that Christ of all God created the world.

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:03.760
What does it mean that He created the world?

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:04.760
It means something very simple.

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:10.760
That at one time the world was not created and just out of the blue, God decided to create

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:15.340
Which means God was not forced by anyone to create the world.

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:19.740
At one time there was no world, and God decided to do the world.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:25.560
And the same God who decided to do the world, he decided to stop working after seven days.

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:29.580
Which means that God is absolutely omnipotent.

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:31.260
He does whatever he wants to.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:36.200
Now we call, how do we call Shabbat in the Torah?

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:38.280
Shabbat is an oath.

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:39.680
It is an oath.

00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:43.680
It is a sign. What does it mean that the Shabbat is a sign?

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:55.680
That people should pray. Could you, in your own mind, prove to me that God created the world in six days and He stopped in the seven days?

00:21:55.680 --> 00:22:05.680
Could you ever prove it? It's impossible not to. Creation, something from nothing, is so difficult that no human mind could ever prove it one way or the other.

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:11.680
You cannot prove. Well certainly that you cannot prove. It is impossible to prove.

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:19.680
So therefore, how could we know that God in point of fact stopped working in the 7 days?

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:30.680
At the next of faith. God is telling us, if you believe in me, if you believe that what I am saying to you is true, stop working on Shabbat.

00:22:30.680 --> 00:22:35.680
It's like you say to your wife, she tells you sometimes, if you love me, you do this to me.

00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:38.680
The same way.

00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:43.680
Well, it's conversely true because it's a psychological act.

00:22:43.680 --> 00:22:48.680
If you believe in him, you do this. Because you cannot understand it.

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:51.680
Somebody says, well, what happens if I understand that world was created?

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:55.680
You can never prove it. It's only an act of faith.

00:22:55.680 --> 00:23:00.180
And because it has an extra face, God says, well, if you're actually in point of fact,

00:23:00.840 --> 00:23:04.880
you believe that I'm omnipotent, I'm all-powerful, etc., etc.,

00:23:04.880 --> 00:23:06.320
you stop working on the path.

00:23:06.640 --> 00:23:07.860
And there is no excuse on the path.

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:09.380
You can't say, well, it's my job, or my this or that.

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:13.080
If you believe that God is omnipotent, then there is no room for any kind of support.

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:16.740
So that is the whole idea of the path, as it is brought here.

00:23:16.740 --> 00:23:19.260
In other words, we believe in the path.

00:23:19.660 --> 00:23:23.400
By fulfilling the path, we declare, not with words,

00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:26.080
but with complete actions

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:26.980
that, you know,

00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:28.600
once I had to speak to ladies,

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:30.060
a group of ladies,

00:23:30.460 --> 00:23:31.460
and I had to explain the Shabbat.

00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:33.620
And I was telling them

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:34.580
this explanation,

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:36.700
what happened if I believe

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:37.700
in my own mind,

00:23:37.780 --> 00:23:38.440
I believe it,

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:40.420
and, but, you know,

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:41.240
I'm not going to do this.

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:42.360
So I said,

00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:43.580
there were ladies,

00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:44.140
you know,

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:46.480
there's two concepts of love.

00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:47.800
There's the Jewish concept of love

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:48.980
and there's the Gori concept of love.

00:23:49.380 --> 00:23:49.960
The Jewish concept of love

00:23:49.960 --> 00:23:50.820
is love has to be

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:53.020
expressed in complete actions.

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:57.800
The going concept of love is love is mainly what you believe, what you feel, and you don't have to show it in your actions.

00:23:58.320 --> 00:24:00.320
Let's say, for instance, say you marry.

00:24:01.020 --> 00:24:03.500
Suppose, you know, there's a husband, say the husband loves his wife.

00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:07.560
There's a kind of husband who will pull around when his wife doesn't know.

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:14.100
And then there is another who says, no, I love her and I'm going to act accordingly.

00:24:14.380 --> 00:24:21.900
So I said, the Jewish concept of Shabbat is that love for God has to be expressed in concrete actions.

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:27.900
There cannot be expressions with words. You have to fulfill and behave accordingly.

00:24:27.900 --> 00:24:33.900
You ladies, you politicians, you know, nobody wants to demand from your husband.

00:24:33.900 --> 00:24:38.900
What kind of love do you demand from your husband? A concrete love, concrete action.

00:24:38.900 --> 00:24:41.900
You see, same thing going on in the mental model.

00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:45.900
Not an abstract, theoretic love, but a concrete action.

00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:47.900
So I think that this expression is a valid expression.

00:24:47.900 --> 00:24:49.900
Nonetheless, we want to continue further.

00:24:49.900 --> 00:24:55.900
And so, Enle Toledotas Oman, they are others, they are the body of God.

00:24:55.900 --> 00:25:04.900
Let me tell you the translation and then I will tell you the answer of the explanation of this translation.

00:25:04.900 --> 00:25:10.900
These are the generations of the heavens and earth at the time of their creation.

00:25:10.900 --> 00:25:16.900
There are two basic explanations. One explanation means Enle refers to the above-mentioned.

00:25:16.900 --> 00:25:20.900
In the above-mentioned way, the world was created.

00:25:20.900 --> 00:25:22.900
Enne toledot ha-shamayim ve'arev.

00:25:22.900 --> 00:25:25.900
In this way, the Shamaim ve'aretz, they came to be.

00:25:25.900 --> 00:25:26.900
Toledo means the generation.

00:25:26.900 --> 00:25:30.900
In this way, the Shamaim ve'aretz were created.

00:25:30.900 --> 00:25:31.900
Enne toledot ha-shamayim ve'arev.

00:25:31.900 --> 00:25:32.900
Ve'arem.

00:25:32.900 --> 00:25:35.900
Enne means in the way that we describe in the specific chapter.

00:25:35.900 --> 00:25:36.900
All right?

00:25:36.900 --> 00:25:38.900
Which is why.

00:25:38.900 --> 00:25:41.900
There's another expression which I prefer in the theory.

00:25:41.900 --> 00:25:43.900
Enne toledot ha-shamayim ve'arev ve'arem.

00:25:43.900 --> 00:25:53.900
Let's see the future, next chapter. This chapter will tell you what happened to Shama and the Ahareb after the creation.

00:25:53.900 --> 00:25:59.900
So, the two explanations, which one can explain, either way, any way you want it.

00:25:59.900 --> 00:26:07.900
One can explain that the letter of Shama and the Ahareb refers to the above chapter.

00:26:07.900 --> 00:26:12.240
In the aforementioned way, Shaman of Aharef came to be.

00:26:12.840 --> 00:26:14.300
Rabbi Abraham Ben-Adra says no.

00:26:15.100 --> 00:26:18.260
And then Shaman of Aharef refers to the next chapter, to chapter 2.

00:26:19.320 --> 00:26:21.280
You're going to see what happened to Shaman of Aharef.

00:26:21.280 --> 00:26:25.560
And what you're going to see, according to Ben-Adra, is that Adam sinned.

00:26:25.560 --> 00:26:28.900
Because Adam changed, there was a change in Shaman of Aharef.

00:26:30.940 --> 00:26:33.060
Now with the Shaman of Aharef, the world changed.

00:26:33.200 --> 00:26:34.640
And why is it important to say this?

00:26:34.640 --> 00:26:41.440
Because if you remember in Basuk 31 of the Siddhim chapter it says,

00:26:41.440 --> 00:26:44.040
Vaya yeh noevi kolash yeh asa ve'in etov me'od

00:26:44.040 --> 00:26:50.040
That that's for everything that it was created and it was very good.

00:26:50.040 --> 00:26:57.240
So if everything that is created is very good, how come that we have so much trouble in the world?

00:26:57.240 --> 00:26:59.640
How come we have so many problems?

00:26:59.640 --> 00:27:00.940
He created us very good.

00:27:00.940 --> 00:27:03.400
Oh, so that's why, that's even harder.

00:27:03.940 --> 00:27:05.640
That's why he's telling you now that

00:27:05.640 --> 00:27:09.140
now you're going to see what happened.

00:27:09.640 --> 00:27:11.420
At one time there was so many odds,

00:27:11.800 --> 00:27:15.180
but then men changed this so many odds.

00:27:16.220 --> 00:27:20.460
And therefore the function of the second chapter,

00:27:20.560 --> 00:27:21.940
of this chapter, is to teach you

00:27:21.940 --> 00:27:24.920
how come that at one time there was so many odds,

00:27:24.920 --> 00:27:27.420
and right now we don't find that so many odds.

00:27:27.660 --> 00:27:28.180
Do you, gentlemen?

00:27:30.940 --> 00:27:43.500
There are many, many, but nobody knows the actual history.

00:27:43.500 --> 00:27:48.960
I wrote an article, by the way, it's explaining all, you know, mentioning all the places in

00:27:48.960 --> 00:27:54.760
the Torah, in the whole Torah, where there is an occult biologic from God.

00:27:54.760 --> 00:27:58.760
I mentioned it and I failed but I don't take it seriously.

00:27:58.760 --> 00:28:00.760
I don't.

00:28:00.760 --> 00:28:02.760
I don't take it seriously what he wrote.

00:28:02.760 --> 00:28:04.760
Yes, but it's all there.

00:28:06.760 --> 00:28:08.760
Also, if you put it up, it gets down.

00:28:14.760 --> 00:28:17.760
Evil would be the absence of the good.

00:28:17.760 --> 00:28:19.760
